{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/linkersets\/declaringakind"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"LinkerSets"}],"role":"article","title":"Declaring a kind"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/UniqueKeys","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/ReplacingARegistry","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/Performance"],"anchor":"Guides","generated":true,"title":"Guides"}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A kind is a 32-bit number that every record carries. A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/documentation\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/LinkerSet","type":"reference"},{"text":" of a kind holds the records","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"declared with that kind and no others, so one program can hold your routes, another library’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"analytics events and a third’s migrations without any of them seeing the others.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Choosing the number","anchor":"Choosing-the-number","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Any number other than 0 works. 0 marks an empty slot, and the macros refuse it. The convention is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"four ASCII letters that name the thing, read as one byte each: “rout” is ","type":"text"},{"code":"r","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"o","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"u","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"t","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"0x72","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"0x6F","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"0x75","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"0x74","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so the kind is ","type":"text"},{"code":"0x726F_7574","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The letters make it unlikely that two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"libraries pick the same number, and they stay readable in a hex dump of the binary. Swift computes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one for you:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let kind = \"rout\".utf8.reduce(0) { $0 << 8 | UInt32($1) }  \/\/ 0x726F_7574"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Give the kind a name for the code that reads it:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["extension LinkerSetKind {","    static let routes = LinkerSetKind(rawValue: 0x726F_7574)  \/\/ \"rout\"","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A library that reads the set for its users keeps the name internal: the macro writes the kind as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"number, so its users’ files never need it."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"When two libraries pick the same number","anchor":"When-two-libraries-pick-the-same-number","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No compiler sees every module at once, so nothing can check that a kind is unique. If two libraries"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"choose the same number, their records land in the same set. A record still hands over its value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only when asked for its own type, so a set of a type your library owns ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Route"},{"type":"text","text":", not "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"String"},{"type":"text","text":")"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"holds only your declarations. Read your records as a type of your own, and a clash costs nothing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"but the time to skip the other library’s records."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Within a kind, records may share any value. To make two declarations of the same route or event","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"name fail to build, give each a unique key: ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/UniqueKeys","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Writing the kind at each declaration","anchor":"Writing-the-kind-at-each-declaration","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/LinkerSetEntry(kind:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" takes the kind as an integer literal. It has to be a literal because the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"macro writes it into the binary at compile time; a named constant isn’t visible to the macro:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["enum Routes {","    @LinkerSetEntry(kind: 0x726F_7574)  \/\/ \"rout\"","    static let home = Route(path: \"\/\")","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"That suits a kind used in a few places. A typo in the number puts the declaration in the wrong","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"set without any error, though.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Giving your users a macro","anchor":"Giving-your-users-a-macro","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A library that asks its users to register things gives them a macro with the kind built in, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"they write ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Route","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and never see the number. The macro lives in a small compiler plugin built on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the LinkerSetsMacroSupport module, whose documentation walks through the plugin, the macro’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"declaration and the package’s targets. The plugin can also require a protocol of every type it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"registers, so ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on a type that isn’t an event fails to compile where it’s written.","type":"text"}]}]}],"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Pick the number that tags your declarations, and decide whether your users write it."}],"references":{"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/LinkerSetEntry(kind:)":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Declares a record of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"kind"},{"text":" whose value is this declaration’s.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"macro"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"LinkerSetEntry"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"kind"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s6UInt32V","text":"UInt32"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"title":"LinkerSetEntry(kind:)","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/LinkerSetEntry(kind:)","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/linkersetentry(kind:)"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/PlatformsAndLinking":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking","type":"topic","title":"Platforms and linking","role":"article","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where records are found, how, and which test shows it."}],"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/platformsandlinking"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/UniqueKeys":{"role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Make two records of one kind with the same key fail to build, within one executable or library.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"Unique keys","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/UniqueKeys","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/uniquekeys","kind":"article"},"doc://LinkerSetsRuntime/documentation/LinkerSetsRuntime/LinkerSet":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"LinkerSet"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every record of one kind, across every image the program has loaded, and the values they"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"produce."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"LinkerSet"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/linkersetsruntime\/linkerset","title":"LinkerSet","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/documentation\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/LinkerSet"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/ReplacingARegistry":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/ReplacingARegistry","type":"topic","title":"Replacing a hand-written registry","role":"article","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Move a central list of event types, routes or registrations onto declarations that find","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"themselves.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/replacingaregistry"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/FindingRecords":{"role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Read every declaration of a kind, as the type you expect."}],"type":"topic","title":"Finding records","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/findingrecords"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets","type":"topic","title":"LinkerSets","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Declarations that register themselves at compile time and are found at run time across every module a program links.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/Performance":{"role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What records cost as an app grows: nothing at launch, a walk of the records when a set is read,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and a few milliseconds of build time per marked declaration."}],"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/performance","title":"Performance","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/Performance","kind":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/WhatTheMacrosRefuse":{"role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every declaration a record can’t describe is a compile error, with a message that says why."}],"title":"What the macros refuse","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/whatthemacrosrefuse","kind":"article"}}}